0 -16 Td
/F1 8 Tf
( ) Tj
0 -12 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(When two monosyllabic words combine into a compound noun, the tone of) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(the second element frequently undergoes sandhi. A Low tone following a) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(High tone is raised to Mid to prevent extreme pitch leaps within a) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(single phonological word. These tone sandhi rules operate systematically) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(across both spoken discourse and traditional musical poetry.) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 8 Tf
